{"title":"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Jesse cuts a circular paper disk of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> along two radii to form two sectors, the smaller having a central angle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa4de95cc6371d125d5cf773cdd9f9913dd1d8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> degrees. He makes two circular cones, using each sector to form the lateral surface of a cone. What is the ratio of the volume of the smaller cone to that of the larger one?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/9/5691a1ec32689fdef25dce5a8d2535d00594813e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{8}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{4}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{10}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{6}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"422\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let us take the example of the smaller sector: notice that when it is folded into a cone, the radius becomes the slant height, and the circumference of the base of the cone is equal to the length of the sector. This gives us the slant height and radius of the cone's base (which comes from the circumference), and if we want to get the height of the cone, we simply have to do <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/5/75528afd80774aecdfc28bbc7dbe4af7081cc641.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s^2 - r_b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"21\" /> by the Pythagorean theorem, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is the slant height and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/0/cb01353fabf2257b6bde123ad5970eb7891a59b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is the base of the radius. Repeat this process for the larger cone. It is easy to derive that the ratio of the volume of the small cone to that of the large one is simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/c/ffc61fd400bcc229934fb2e87e2e246bb80838b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{r_s^2h_s}{r_l^2h_l}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"40\" height=\"45\" />. \n</p><p>This gives us the answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/9/cb9fe6f6642e5159a5c716d62522e35a2d61f13c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathbf{C}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"28\" height=\"25\" />. \n</p><p>~Prana8v\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the original radius is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, then the circumference is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/7/ca72da509d0e888f69331dc91184a176fef7dae5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />; since arcs are defined by the central angles, the smaller arc, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa4de95cc6371d125d5cf773cdd9f9913dd1d8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> degree angle, is half the size of the larger sector. so the smaller arc is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/b/9fb1c2c9bfe3fc5bca66d58ba9a8cd476ae446d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8\\pi$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />, and the larger is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/6/a8614a7ac3a38794811c563d39185fa13a00d684.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. Those two arc lengths become the two circumferences of the new cones; so the radius of the smaller cone is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the larger cone is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Using the Pythagorean theorem, the height of the larger cone is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/4/3a4896b3f769896054f21691accd1ed331b99961.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\cdot\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" /> and the smaller cone is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/d/2ad4a58de6859e6c5ca4921b2d801d6bc616bf05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8\\cdot\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" />, and now for volume just square the radii and multiply by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/3/c53700c7fb5b8947273bbcdaf696719461fcb124.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"9\" height=\"21\" /> of the height to get the volume of each cone: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/9/f49c25f6486c172dce9f6858be0fefb39f3ba316.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$128\\cdot\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/3/eb3fc9ce070f31b6ca81bf9b818805e4f2bd5e92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$256\\cdot\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> [both multiplied by three as ratio come out the same. now divide the volumes by each other to get the final ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/3/5e3c33b22966c788ece10a9b76e47228806cd455.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } \\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{10}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"84\" height=\"53\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B\">2012 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017230046\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.039 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.052 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 196/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1963/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3914/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    9.580      1 Template:AMC12_box\n100.00%    9.580      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:10772:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017230046 and revision id 290495. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}